# TESTING STANDARDS (apply to every milestone)

- Test pyramid: unit (pure logic, property-based where math is involved), integration (real Postgres/Redis/LiveKit via Compose or Testcontainers), contract (every response validated against `openapi.yaml`; every realtime message validated against its schema), e2e with bots (real keypairs, real devnet), load and chaos.
- Every error code in `errors.json` has at least one test that triggers it.
- Every money-moving path has a conservation test: sum of ledger deltas equals the expected value, and no path can create Cash from nothing.
- Every webhook handler has replay, out-of-order and duplicate tests.
- Flaky tests are bugs. Fix them, do not retry them into passing.
- CI runs lint, typecheck, unit, integration, contract checks, Anchor tests, and codegen freshness on every push. E2E, load and mainnet-read tests run in a separate manual or nightly workflow.

# REPORTING FORMAT

At the end of every milestone, print and append to `docs/TEST_REPORT.md`:
1. Milestone name and commit hash.
2. Exact commands run and their real output (trimmed to pass/fail counts plus any failures).
3. Measured numbers (latency, bandwidth, credit latency, load results).
4. New entries added to `DECISIONS.md`, `UNVERIFIED.md` and `docs/adr/`.
5. Documentation created or updated this milestone, and the result of the docs-check and architecture-boundary checks (both must pass).
6. A short SOLID self-review: any module that exceeds the size limits or crosses a layer boundary, with justification or the refactor you did.
7. Anything in the spec you believe is wrong, inconsistent or risky, with a proposed fix. Do not silently work around spec problems. Flag them.

